& [Selection]
  + preserve official App Server sandbox protocol facts and derive the smallest independent enforcement-evidence candidate for B1 gap G04
  + this inventory does not select or launch an executable configure a sandbox create a canary run a command contact a provider or issue process observation authority

& [OfficialAppServerSurface]
  + [page] https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/app-server.md is the official Codex App Server page captured on 2026-08-23
  + turn/start accepts approval and sandbox overrides while turn/steer does not accept sandbox overrides
  + supported sandboxPolicy types include dangerFullAccess readOnly workspaceWrite and externalSandbox
  + readOnly can carry explicit read-access controls and workspaceWrite can carry writable roots read-only access controls and network access
  + command/exec runs one argv command under the server sandbox without starting a thread or turn and accepts a sandboxPolicy deadline and bounded streaming controls
  + thread/shellCommand explicitly runs outside the sandbox with full access and does not inherit the thread policy
  + experimental process/spawn explicitly runs outside the sandbox and requires experimentalApi capability
  + externalSandbox tells Codex to skip its own sandbox enforcement because another boundary is presumed
  + windowsSandbox/setupStart asynchronously requests elevated or unelevated setup and windowsSandbox/setupCompleted reports setup outcome
  + permissionProfile/list and configRequirements/read expose available policy and managed-requirement state but are configuration reports rather than independent effect observations

& [OfficialEnforcementContext]
  + [page] https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/sandboxing.md is the official cross-client sandbox page captured on 2026-08-23
  + sandboxing and approval are separate controls: the sandbox defines technical boundaries while approval policy defines when boundary crossing must stop for consent
  + sandbox policy applies to spawned commands and their children rather than only built-in file operations
  + official documentation describes platform-native enforcement and identifies native Windows sandboxing for PowerShell and Linux sandboxing for WSL2
  + [page] https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/windows/windows-sandbox.md is the official native Windows sandbox page captured on 2026-08-23
  + native Windows offers stronger elevated setup and fallback unelevated setup with different enforcement strength
  + setup completion policy echo successful request return or documentation claim does not independently prove the selected current binary enforced one attempted boundary

& [B1ProtocolDenials]
  + forbid dangerFullAccess externalSandbox thread/shellCommand process/spawn experimentalApi and any method whose declared semantics bypass the sandbox
  + forbid turn/start model work MCP startup browser connector web search and other surfaces whose service traffic or side effects are outside local command sandbox proof
  + permit only initialization required schema reconciliation configuration reads that cannot mutate and one separately commissioned command/exec enforcement probe
  + use approval policy never only together with a deny-by-construction method allowlist so an unexpected request refuses rather than escalating
  + bind the exact sandboxPolicy request response method sequence capability set and generated-schema digest to the selected executable commission

& [IndependentEnforcementEvidenceCandidate]
  + create all probe fixtures only inside separately admitted disposable roots with an exact cleanup and recovery owner under G06
  + before launch an independent host observer records content digest metadata and existence for readable canaries denied-read canaries workspace-write canaries outside-root canaries and state roots
  + command/exec receives an exact readOnly policy with the smallest admitted readable-root set and network disabled by the exact selected schema grammar
  + the bounded probe attempts one allowed read and explicit denied reads and writes using fixed argv without shell expansion user input provider or repository mutation
  + the App Server response must report refusal for denied operations and bounded success only for the allowed read
  + after descendant termination the independent host observer remeasures every canary and refuses any bytes metadata existence root or descendant drift
  + enforcement proof requires both protocol refusal and unchanged independent post-state; either one alone is insufficient
  + network refusal needs an independently observed local-only fixture or platform trace that creates no external contact and must be separately specified rather than inferred from a false remote attempt
  + windowsSandbox setup identity actual elevated-versus-unelevated mode and enforcement capability must be bound independently of a success notification

& [Delineation]
  + sandboxPolicy is a requested protocol object and not itself an enforcement receipt
  + command/exec is the only documented bounded in-sandbox process primitive suitable for a B1 enforcement probe
  + thread/shellCommand process/spawn and externalSandbox are explicit authority escapes and cannot be reachable from the B1 carrier
  + app-server authentication model and other client service traffic are outside spawned-command sandbox guarantees so B1 must remain provider-free and method-closed
  + readOnly does not prove zero state writes by the outer app-server process which is why disposable CODEX_HOME and CODEX_SQLITE_HOME roots remain separately required

& [GapDelta]
  + G04 changes from unspecified sandbox response and enforcement proof to exact admissible and forbidden App Server method families plus a dual protocol-and-host canary proof candidate
  + G04 remains unresolved for the selected binary schema exact policy encoding Windows setup identity canary grammar independent observer and live refusal receipts
  + G05 is narrowed to a method-closed carrier that cannot represent thread/shellCommand process/spawn externalSandbox dangerFullAccess experimentalApi or turn/model work but its Rust type is not yet specified
  + G06 remains unresolved for exact disposable roots pre-state cleanup recovery and owner
  + G01 G02 G03 and G07 retain their prior states

& [StopRules]
  + do not launch codex app-server command/exec windowsSandbox setup shellCommand process/spawn provider model MCP browser connector or network transport
  + do not create modify or delete a sandbox permission profile canary state root firewall rule account ACL or repository path
  + do not treat a requested policy echoed response setup success or official claim as independent host-enforcement proof
  + do not use a remote network attempt to prove denial

& [Next]
  + hash and manifest this sandbox inventory
  + preserve G04 as narrowed_not_closed and G05 as narrowed_not_closed
  + after governed executable selection and exact generated schema commission the provider-free canary fixture observer and method-closed carrier separately
